{"name":"In the Shadows","hex":"#cbc4c0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"shadows","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of shadow"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of shadow"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shadows"}],"entries":[{"title":"In the Shadow (2012 film)","blocks":[{"text":"In the Shadow is a 2012 Czech crime film directed by David Ondříček. The film was selected as the Czech entry for the Best Foreign Language Oscar at the 85th Academy Awards, but it did not make the final shortlist."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a3/In_the_Shadow_%282012_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_the_Shadow_(2012_film)","wikidata":"Q5817326"},{"title":"In the Shadows (2001 film)","blocks":[{"text":"In the Shadows is a 2001 American thriller film written and directed by Ric Roman Waugh and starring Matthew Modine, James Caan, Joey Lauren Adams, Lillo Brancato and Cuba Gooding Jr. It was released in the United States on June 22, 2001. In the film, Modine plays hit man Eric O'Bryne, who is sent to kill veteran Hollywood stuntman Lance Huston (Caan), falls in love with the target's daughter (Adams) and then decides to become a stuntman himself."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/93/In_the_Shadows_%282001_film%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_the_Shadows_(2001_film)","wikidata":"Q1473609"},{"title":"In the Shadows (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"In the Shadows\" is a song by Finnish alternative rock band the Rasmus, included on the group's fifth studio album, Dead Letters (2003). Released in Finland in January 2003, the single achieved considerable chart success throughout Europe and Oceania, topping the charts of Finland, Germany, Hungary, and New Zealand and peaking at No. 3 in the United Kingdom. It was also successful in South America, reaching No. 1 in Bolivia, Chile, and Paraguay. The song was nominated for the Kerrang! Award for Best Single in 2004."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/Rasmus-In_the_shadows.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/In_the_Shadows_(song)","wikidata":"Q2603982"},{"title":"Shadow","blocks":[{"text":"A shadow is a dark area on a surface where light from a light source is blocked by an object. In contrast, shade occupies the three-dimensional volume behind an object with light in front of it. The cross-section of a shadow is a two-dimensional silhouette, or a reverse projection of the object blocking the light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg/330px-The_shadow_of_a_musician_playing_transverse_flute.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shadow","wikidata":"Q160020"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Park_grid.JPG/500px-Park_grid.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Park_grid.JPG/1280px-Park_grid.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Park_grid.JPG/500px-Park_grid.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Park fence shadow is distorted by an uneven snow surface.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APark_grid.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Cumulus_cloud_shadows_1.jpg/500px-Cumulus_cloud_shadows_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedi